lementation**: lightweight `ExportApiClient` proxies registered for browser environments that delegate to server API routes.\\n  16 \\n  17 ### 4. Browser-Only Dynamic Synthesis Pattern\\n  18 **Purpose**: Handling libraries with mandatory DOM dependencies (e.g., `pptxgenjs`) within a Next.js 15 environment.\\n  19 - **Implementation**: Moving synthesis logic entirely to client hooks using dynamic `import()` to prevent server-side reference errors.\\n  20 \\n  21 ## State & Data Patterns\\n  22 \\n  23 ### 1. Auth Status Vector Pattern\\n  24 **Purpose**: ensuring predictable UI transitions and hydration safety.\\n  25 - **Implementation**: A unified `AuthStatus` union (`loading`, `authenticated`, `unauthenticated`, `guest`, `error`) in `AuthContext`.\\n  26 \\n  27 ### 2. Atomic Mapping & Transformation\\n  28 **Purpose**: Preventing domain contamination and race conditions.\\n  29 - **Pattern**: Selective property mapping in form submissions and `targets.reduce(...)` within single store callbacks for multi-node updates.\\n  30 \\n  31 ### 3. Neural Telemetry & Monitoring\\n  32 **Purpose**: Real-time observability of AI pipeline performance.\\n  33 - **Implementation**: High-precision timing instrumented across Embedding, Search, and Reranking phases.\\n  34 \\n  35 ## Robustness & Resilience Patterns\\n  36 \\n  37 ### 1. Unified Existence Guard Pattern\\n  38 **Purpose**: Preventing runtime crashes on partially hydrated or null state.\\n  39 - **Implementation**: Explicit `if (!entity)` patterns in all interaction and persistence handlers.\\n  40 \\n  41 ### 2. Neural Error Boundary Pattern\\n  42 **Purpose**: Containing failures within specific UI zones.\\n  43 - **Implementation**: `RendererErrorBoundary` wrapped around the document canvas and analysis hubs.\\n  44 \\n  45 ### 3. Selection Recovery Pattern\\n  46 **Purpose**: Synchronizing structural shifts with UI interaction states.\\n  47 - **Implementation**: Automated sweeps that clear active focuses when nodes are deleted.\\n  48 \\n  49 ## UI/UX & Aesthetics\\n  50 \\n  51 ### 1. Intelligence Suite Aesthetic\\n  52 **Purpose**: Professional technical \\"IDE-style\\" interaction model.\\n  53 - **Standard**: 28px dot-grids, high-density labels (`text-[10px]`, `font-black`, `uppercase`), and glassmorphism.\\n  54 \\n  55 ### 2. Stable Manifest Footer\\n  56 **Purpose**: Providing version context and operational status.\\n  57 - **Pattern**: Standardized footers (`v2.4.0-STABLE`) across all HUD and monitoring panels.\\n  58 \\n````","Successfully opened memory-bank/techContext.md:\\n\\n````markdown\\n   0 # Technical Context - Arkan\\n   1 \\n   2 ## Technology Stack\\n   3 \\n   4 ### Frontend Framework\\n   5 - **Next.js 15**: React-based full-stack framework.\\n   6 - **React 19**: Standardized top-level hook placement for stable concurrent rendering.\\n   7 - **TypeScript**: Strict-mode type safety with 100% compliance verified via `tsc`.\\n   8 \\n   9 ### AI Integration\\n  10 - **Google Genkit**: Core AI orchestration framework.\\n  11 - **Ollama**: Local neural inference cluster.\\n  12 - **Result Pattern**: Uniform `Result<T, E>` return vectors for all flows.\\n  13 - **Telemetry**: High-precision timing instrumentation for all retrieval phases.\\n  14 \\n  15 ### Data & Visualization\\n  16 - **Database**: SQLite with Drizzle ORM.\\n  17 - **Vector Database**: Qdrant (`arkan_vectors` collection, 768 dims).\\n  18 - **Analytics**: **Recharts** for real-time performance and latency tracking.\\n  19 \\n  20 ### UI Framework\\n  21 - **shadcn/ui**: Built on Radix UI and Tailwind CSS.\\n  22 - **Intelligence Suite Aesthetic**: High-density typography, 28px technical grids, and pulsing status nodes.\\n  23 \\n  24 ## Architecture Patterns\\n  25 \\n  26 ### Dependency Injection (DI)\\n  27 - **tsyringe**: Registered in `container.ts`.\\n  28 - **Bridging Pattern**: API Client proxies for browser-side DI resolution.\\n  29 \\n  30 ### RAG Architecture\\n  31 - **Performance**: Sub-100ms retrieval achieved via bitwise string hashing, lazy vector store initialization, and O(N) result merging.\\n  32 - **Resilience**: Hybrid reranking guards and multi-layer LRU caching for embeddings and search results.\\n  33 \\n  34 ### Security Architecture\\n  35 - **Auth Node**: Local JWT-based sessions with hardware fingerprinting.\\n  36 - **Transmission**: Universal use of `try-catch` blocks and structured error feedback across all procurement and authentication vectors.\\n  37 \\n````","Successfully opened memory-bank/recentUpdates.md:\\n\\n````markdown\\n   0 # Recent Updates - Arkan Memory Bank\\n   1 \\n   2 *Last Updated: April 2026*\\n   3 \\n   4 ## April 2026 Updates\\n   5 \\n   6 ### **Global Robustness Hardening & UI Standardization**\\n   7 **Date**: April 2026\\n   8 **Summary**: Completed an intensive application-wide hardening pass across 60+ core components to ensure production-grade stability and Next.js 15 compliance.\\n   9 \\n  10 - **Foundational Layout & Auth**: Hardened `AuthContext` with a unified status vector and established the \\"Intelligence Suite\\" aesthetic in the global `Header`.\\n  11 - **Administrative Table Hardening**: Refactored `SectionDataTable` and `TemplateManagementConsole` with defensive row mapping and high-fidelity empty states.\\n  12 - **Form Manifest Purity**: Hardened `SectionFormDialog` and Profile forms with atomic property mapping to prevent domain contamination.\\n  13 - **Writing Tool Resilience**: Migrated tool hooks to the `Result` pattern and implemented \\"Neural Buffer\\" guards to prevent concurrent AI transmissions.\\n  14 - **SEO & Discovery**: Implemented JSON-LD structured data, dynamic sitemaps, and optimized production `robots.ts` for public tool discoverability.\\n  15 - **RAG Overhaul**: Achieved sub-100ms retrieval latency via bitwise hashing and lazy initialization. established a mission-control monitoring suite with Recharts analytics.\\n  16 - **PPTX Engine Stabilization**: Fixed environment crashes by migrating browser-dependent synthesis logic entirely to the client-side.\\n  17 \\n  18 ## March 2026 Updates\\n  19 \\n  20 ### **AI Resilience & Domain Hardening**\\n  21 - **Tiered Fallback Logic**: Implemented automated model degradation (Llama 3 → Phi-3 → Gemma 2B) to ensure 8GB RAM stability.\\n  22 - **Standardized Entity Pattern**: Unified all domain entities on the `toProperties()` and `withProps()` pattern.\\n  23 - **Clean Architecture Implementation**: Reached 100% DDD compliance across all modules.\\n  24 \\n````"]'}
